IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: ss 172, 172A and 172B -- provisions protecting officers from liability, insurance, and third party indemnity.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Part sgb2. Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.
--
-- HOW IT READS. A provision that exempts an officer from liability for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust towards the company is void (s 172(1)); so is a provision by which the company indemnifies an
-- officer against such liability, except as ss 172A and 172B permit (s 172(2)). The company may buy insurance for an officer (s 172A). The company may indemnify an officer against liability to someone else, except a
-- criminal fine, a regulatory penalty, the cost of defending criminal proceedings that end in conviction, the cost of defending a civil claim by the company or a related company that ends in judgment against the officer,
-- and an application for relief the court refuses (s 172B(1)). The conviction, judgment or refusal counts only when final (s 172B(2) and (3)). No penalty is stated: the sections void a provision and carry no offence.
-- Whether a corporation is related to the company (s 6), and who is an "officer" (s 4(1)), are facts here.

§ `Section 172(1) to (3): provisions that are void`

DECLARE `s 172(3) where the provision is contained` IS ONE OF
    `s 172(3) in the company's constitution`
    `s 172(3) in a contract with the company`
    `s 172(3) otherwise`

-- (1): "Any provision that purports to exempt an officer of a company (to any extent) from any liability that would otherwise attach to him or her in connection with any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of
-- trust in relation to the company is void."
-- src:14659 | 172.—(1) Any provision that purports to exempt an officer of a
-- src:14660 | company (to any extent) from any liability that would otherwise
-- src:14661 | attach to him or her in connection with any negligence, default,
-- src:14662 | breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company is void.
@ref s 172(1) (src:14659-14662)
GIVEN `the provision purports to exempt an officer of the company (to any extent) from a liability that would otherwise attach to the officer in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172(1) the provision purporting to exempt an officer from liability is void` MEANS
    IF `the provision purports to exempt an officer of the company (to any extent) from a liability that would otherwise attach to the officer in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any provision that purports to exempt an officer ... from any liability that would otherwise attach ... in connection with any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company is void" says which provisions are void and says nothing of any other provision

-- (2): "Any provision by which a company directly or indirectly provides an indemnity (to any extent) for an officer of the company against any liability attaching to him or her in connection with any negligence,
-- default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company is void, except as permitted by section 172A or 172B."
-- src:14666 | (2) Any provision by which a company directly or indirectly
-- src:14667 | provides an indemnity (to any extent) for an officer of the company
-- src:14668 | against any liability attaching to him or her in connection with any
-- src:14673 | negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the
-- src:14674 | company is void, except as permitted by section 172A or 172B.
@ref s 172(2) (src:14666-14674)
GIVEN `the provision is one by which the company directly or indirectly provides an indemnity (to any extent) for an officer of the company against a liability attaching to the officer in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is permitted by section 172A or 172B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172(2) the provision for an indemnity is void` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the provision is one by which the company directly or indirectly provides an indemnity (to any extent) for an officer of the company against a liability attaching to the officer in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any provision by which a company directly or indirectly provides an indemnity (to any extent) for an officer of the company against any liability attaching to him or her in connection with any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company is void" says which provisions are void and says nothing of any other provision
    ELSE IF `the provision is permitted by section 172A or 172B`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is void, except as permitted by section 172A or 172B" (an "except" once met: the Guide's "In short" line, which lists plain variants such as while, until and except)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (3): "This section applies to any provision, whether contained in a company's constitution or in any contract with the company or otherwise." The three places are one list closed by "or otherwise": every place is covered.
-- src:14678 | (3) This section applies to any provision, whether contained in a
-- src:14679 | company’s constitution or in any contract with the company or
-- src:14680 | otherwise.
@ref s 172(3) (src:14678-14680)
GIVEN place IS A `s 172(3) where the provision is contained`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172(3) the section applies to the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `s 172(3) in the company's constitution` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 172(3) in a contract with the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 172(3) otherwise` THEN JUST TRUE

§ `Section 172A: insurance`

-- "Section 172(2) does not prevent a company from purchasing and maintaining for an officer of the company insurance against any such liability mentioned in that subsection."
-- Named for the exception (fork F-163-0): JUST TRUE reads "within the exception", NOTHING reads "the text does not say".
-- src:14686 | 172A. Section 172(2) does not prevent a company from purchasing
-- src:14687 | and maintaining for an officer of the company insurance against any
-- src:14688 | such liability mentioned in that subsection.
@ref s 172A (src:14686-14688)
GIVEN `the company purchases and maintains for an officer of the company insurance against a liability mentioned in section 172(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172A the insurance is within the exception from section 172(2)` MEANS
    IF `the company purchases and maintains for an officer of the company insurance against a liability mentioned in section 172(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 172(2) does not prevent a company from purchasing and maintaining for an officer of the company insurance against any such liability" names insurance and says nothing of any other arrangement

§ `Section 172B: third party indemnity`

-- (1): "Section 172(2) does not apply where the provision for indemnity is against liability incurred by the officer to a person other than the company, except when the indemnity is against (a) any liability of the officer
-- to pay (i) a fine in criminal proceedings; or (ii) a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with any requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising); or (b) any
-- liability incurred by the officer (i) in defending criminal proceedings in which he or she is convicted; (ii) in defending civil proceedings brought by the company or a company that is deemed to be related to the company
-- by virtue of section 6, in which judgment is given against him or her; or (iii) in connection with an application for relief referred to in subsection (4) in which the court refuses to grant him or her relief."
-- The conviction, judgment and refusal are the final decision ((2), (3)), a fact each (b) input carries.
-- src:14694 | 172B.—(1) Section 172(2) does not apply where the provision for
-- src:14695 | indemnity is against liability incurred by the officer to a person other
-- src:14696 | than the company, except when the indemnity is against —
-- src:14698 | (a) any liability of the officer to pay —
-- src:14700 | (i) a fine in criminal proceedings; or
-- src:14702 | (ii) a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a
-- src:14703 | penalty in respect of non‑compliance with any
-- src:14704 | requirement of a regulatory nature (however
-- src:14705 | arising); or
-- src:14707 | (b) any liability incurred by the officer —
-- src:14709 | (i) in defending criminal proceedings in which he or she
-- src:14710 | is convicted;
-- src:14712 | (ii) in defending civil proceedings brought by the
-- src:14713 | company or a company that is deemed to be
-- src:14714 | related to the company by virtue of section 6, in
-- src:14715 | which judgment is given against him or her; or
-- src:14719 | (iii) in connection with an application for relief referred
-- src:14720 | to in subsection (4) in which the court refuses to
-- src:14721 | grant him or her relief.
@ref s 172B(1) (src:14694-14721)
GIVEN `the indemnity is against liability incurred by the officer to a person other than the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indemnity is against a liability of the officer to pay a fine in criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indemnity is against a liability of the officer to pay a sum to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with a requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indemnity is against a liability incurred by the officer in defending criminal proceedings in which the officer is convicted, the conviction being the final decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indemnity is against a liability incurred by the officer in defending civil proceedings brought by the company or by a company deemed by section 6 to be related to it, in which judgment is given against the officer as the final decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indemnity is against a liability incurred by the officer in connection with an application for relief referred to in subsection (4) in which the court refuses to grant relief as the final decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172B(1) the provision for indemnity is within the exception from section 172(2)` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the indemnity is against liability incurred by the officer to a person other than the company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 172(2) does not apply where the provision for indemnity is against liability incurred by the officer to a person other than the company" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork F-172B-1 in NOTES.md)
    ELSE IF    `the indemnity is against a liability of the officer to pay a fine in criminal proceedings`
            OR `the indemnity is against a liability of the officer to pay a sum to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with a requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising)`
            OR `the indemnity is against a liability incurred by the officer in defending criminal proceedings in which the officer is convicted, the conviction being the final decision`
            OR `the indemnity is against a liability incurred by the officer in defending civil proceedings brought by the company or by a company deemed by section 6 to be related to it, in which judgment is given against the officer as the final decision`
            OR `the indemnity is against a liability incurred by the officer in connection with an application for relief referred to in subsection (4) in which the court refuses to grant relief as the final decision`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except when the indemnity is against (a) ... or (b) ..." (an "except" once met: the Guide's "In short" line, which lists plain variants such as while, until and except)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (3)(a): a conviction, judgment or refusal of relief becomes final "(i) if it is not appealed against -- at the end of the period for bringing an appeal; or (ii) if it is appealed against -- at the time when the appeal
-- (or any further appeal) is disposed of". The period for bringing an appeal is another law's, so its last day is an input.
-- src:14735 | (a) a conviction, judgment or refusal of relief becomes final —
-- src:14737 | (i) if it is not appealed against — at the end of the period
-- src:14738 | for bringing an appeal; or
-- src:14740 | (ii) if it is appealed against — at the time when the
-- src:14741 | appeal (or any further appeal) is disposed of; and
@ref s 172B(3)(a) (src:14735-14741)
GIVEN `the decision was appealed against` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the period for bringing an appeal` IS A DATE
      `the day the appeal (or any further appeal) was disposed of` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 172B(3)(a) the day the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief becomes final` MEANS
    IF `the decision was appealed against`
    THEN `the day the appeal (or any further appeal) was disposed of`
    ELSE `the last day of the period for bringing an appeal`

-- (3)(b): an appeal (or further appeal) is disposed of "(i) if it is determined and there is no right of further appeal, or if there is a right of further appeal, the period for bringing any further appeal has ended; or
-- (ii) if it is abandoned or otherwise ceases to have effect". The day is the day it is determined, or the last day of the period for a further appeal, or the day it was abandoned (fork F-172B-3).
DECLARE `s 172B(3)(b) how the appeal ended` IS ONE OF
    `s 172B(3)(b)(i) it was determined`
    `s 172B(3)(b)(ii) it was abandoned or otherwise ceased to have effect`

-- src:14743 | (b) an appeal (or further appeal) is disposed of —
-- src:14745 | (i) if it is determined and there is no right of further
-- src:14746 | appeal, or if there is a right of further appeal, the
-- src:14747 | period for bringing any further appeal has ended; or
-- src:14749 | (ii) if it is abandoned or otherwise ceases to have effect.
@ref s 172B(3)(b) (src:14743-14749)
GIVEN how IS A `s 172B(3)(b) how the appeal ended`
      `the day the appeal was determined` IS A DATE
      `there is a right of further appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the period for bringing any further appeal` IS A DATE
      `the day the appeal was abandoned or otherwise ceased to have effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 172B(3)(b) the day the appeal (or further appeal) is disposed of` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `s 172B(3)(b)(i) it was determined`
         THEN (IF `there is a right of further appeal` THEN `the last day of the period for bringing any further appeal` ELSE `the day the appeal was determined`)
    WHEN `s 172B(3)(b)(ii) it was abandoned or otherwise ceased to have effect` THEN `the day the appeal was abandoned or otherwise ceased to have effect`

-- (2): "The references in subsection (1)(b) to a conviction, judgment or refusal of relief are references to the final decision in the proceedings."
-- src:14728 | (2) The references in subsection (1)(b) to a conviction, judgment or
-- src:14729 | refusal of relief are references to the final decision in the proceedings.
@ref s 172B(2) (src:14728-14729)
GIVEN `the day the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief becomes final` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172B(2) the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief is the final decision on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day in question` AT LEAST `the day the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief becomes final`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The references in subsection (1)(b) to a conviction, judgment or refusal of relief are references to the final decision in the proceedings" and (3) says when a decision "becomes final" (a decision that has not yet become final is not the final decision)

-- (4): "The reference in subsection (1)(b)(iii) to an application for relief is to an application for relief under section 76A(13) or 391."
-- src:14753 | (4) The reference in subsection (1)(b)(iii) to an application for relief
-- src:14754 | is to an application for relief under section 76A(13) or 391.
@ref s 172B(4) (src:14753-14754)
GIVEN `the application is an application for relief under section 76A(13)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is an application for relief under section 391` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172B(4) the application is an application for relief referred to in subsection (1)(b)(iii)` MEANS
    IF `the application is an application for relief under section 76A(13)` OR `the application is an application for relief under section 391`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The reference in subsection (1)(b)(iii) to an application for relief is to an application for relief under section 76A(13) or 391" (read as a definition that fixes what is meant: fork F-162-12, read the same way)
